# sm_120 Level-2 native: compiler-declared extended-parameter metadata extender
#
# Opt-in (XG_NATIVE_META_EXTEND, presence-based, default off). At the four
# module-load entry points of the shim (cuModuleLoadData{,Ex},
# cuModuleLoadFatBinary, cuLibraryLoadData) the image is copied and, for
# every sm_120 kernel whose EIATTR_PARAM_CBANK declares param_start 0x380
# with a smaller extent, both compiler-written extent records are raised to
# 0x1520 so the window-args relay blob matches the declared c[0x0] param
# extent: EIATTR_CBANK_PARAM_SIZE (nvinfo id 0x19, fmt 3) and the
# EIATTR_PARAM_CBANK param_size (id 0x0a, fmt 4). KPARAM_INFO (app args)
# and all other records/sections stay byte-identical. Fail-open on every
# anomaly; idempotent.
#
# Files (isolated native source tree, shim only):
#   platforms/cuda/shim/src/window_meta_extend.cpp            (new)
#   platforms/cuda/shim/include/xsched/cuda/shim/window_meta_extend.h (new)
#   platforms/cuda/shim/src/intercept.cpp                     (4 hooks)
# The runner change (forwarding XG_NATIVE_META_EXTEND to the workers,
# see native_worker_env in workloads/xsched/level2/native/run_native_blob.py)
# is maintained directly in the main repository, not in this patch.
#
# SECOND OPT-IN XG_NATIVE_META_KPARAM (KPARAM_INFO ordinal growth): raises
# the max declared ordinal end so it covers the 0x1520 relay blob. Causal
# evidence (build owner's driver-entry control, raw HX4CV3, same installed
# binary, original entry selected): changing only the relay CU_LAUNCH_PARAM
# BUFFER_SIZE from 0x1520 to the original compute size 0x20 at the real
# driver cuLaunchKernel entry makes all 200 queued kernels launch ret 0 and
# the BE complete and exit cleanly (outputs validated); the full-size relay
# fails the first launch with 701 (kv7jHZ, NmlhJN). The declared ordinal
# extent (0x20) is the remaining candidate the driver checks against the
# buffer. CONSTRAINT: the grown ordinals are safe only for blob-form
# launches (extra buffer, params == nullptr); a plain kernelParams launch
# marshals per-ordinal using the declared sizes and would copy the grown
# size from the app's own argument pointer. The knob is separate from
# XG_NATIVE_META_EXTEND so a metadata-only control configuration stays
# available. Size-field encoding is inferred from 5 observed records
# (size*4 + 1 for 4-aligned sizes); the grown values are unvalidated until
# the build owner's run. The forwarding for this second variable must be
# added to the runner's worker environment (same pattern as
# XG_NATIVE_META_EXTEND in native_worker_env).
#
# Module images may also arrive wrapped in the CUDA runtime fatbin wrapper
# (__fatBinC_Wrapper_t from fatbinary_section.h: magic 0x466243b1, version
# 1, whose data field points at the real container). Static cudart passes
# this wrapper to cuLibraryLoadData and the driver follows wrapper->data
# (root gdb evidence: debug-module-image.log in raw aY3rBY). The extender
# recognizes the wrapper and hands the load call one owned block holding a
# wrapper copy in a 32-byte slot (24 bytes used) whose data field is
# retargeted at the patched nested container copy inside the same block,
# so the driver receives the original wrapper ABI except for the owned
# data pointer; one free of the handed-out wrapper pointer covers both.
# Wrapper versions other than 1 and nested payloads that are neither
# fatbin nor cubin pass through unchanged.
#
# Deployment status (build owner, raw NmlhJN): the wrapper route engages
# in the real run - the four BE logs confirm both extent records raised
# (0x8/0x20 -> 0x1520), an owned wrapper copy 0x20 + nested container
# 0x4818 bytes, a successful module load and binary guardian preparation -
# while the first launch still returns 701. The metadata route is reached
# but not sufficient; parameter delivery remains the open failure.
#
# Verified CPU-side on the local priority_workload specimen (no GPU):
# exactly six bytes differ per image (the two extent records of each of the
# two kernels, 0x8/0x20 -> 0x1520); nvdisasm -c and cuobjdump -elf parse the
# patched cubin and patched fatbin and report EIATTR_CBANK_PARAM_SIZE 0x1520
# beside EIATTR_PARAM_CBANK 0x15200380; repeated application is idempotent.
# XgFreeExtendedImage reads the preceding allocation header, so it is NOT
# safe for arbitrary foreign pointers. Memory-safety scrutiny in the
# session did not retain a valgrind artifact file, so no retained-clean
# claim is made. After the wrapper case was added the source compiles as
# g++ -O2 and as -O3 -DRELEASE_MODE -Wall -Wextra -Werror; the wrapper
# path was not CPU-unit-tested before deployment.
#
# BUILD NOTE: window_meta_extend.cpp enters the shim sources via
# file(GLOB_RECURSE) evaluated at CMAKE CONFIGURE time. A build directory
# configured before the file exists silently omits it (observed: nm -D on
# the installed libshimcuda.so showed undefined XgMetaExtendImage/
# XgFreeExtendedImage and all six workers failed before reaching ready).
# Re-run the cmake configure step, then --build --target install.
#
# Experimental and unintegrated until the build owner tests it; this is an
# sm_120 native actuator port, not an unchanged upstream artifact.
# Apply plain: patch -p1 < xsched-native-meta-extend.patch
# from the source root (level2-build/.output/<native dir>/source).
--- /dev/null
